# Security

## Confirmed

- Email/password authentication shall exist (AUTH-10). Values (TTL, provisioning) are not defined.
- Employees access only their own leave/attendance (AUTH-02, AUTH-03, BR-13).
- HR/Admin has org-wide access (AUTH-04, BR-14). `guest_admin` is read-only (AUTH-08/09).
- Employees must not GET medical documents (MED-09).
- Every change belongs in an audit log (BR-12).
- Uploads limited to PDF, JPG, JPEG, PNG (BR-06).

## Always enforce

- Never hardcode secrets. Never commit service-role keys. Use env vars; keep `.env` gitignored.
- Never log passwords, tokens, OTPs, or medical bytes/filenames at info level.
- Validate all external input. Enforce authorization **server-side**. Never trust client-provided role, employee id, or ownership.
- Do not expose whether another employee exists: Proposed convention is 404 (not 403) for employee access to another’s UUID — requires confirmation before coding as policy.
- Rate-limit login and check-in when those endpoints exist (Proposed).

## Approval

Authentication model, authorization/RBAC, and production secret/config changes require human approval.

Details: `documentation/security/model.md`.
